From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:52:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: enable ABI-safe container networking

Enable nftables, bridge netfilter, IPv6 NAT, IPVS, SCTP, VXLAN/VLAN/IPVLAN/MACVLAN, L2TP, FOU, GRE and tc. The added namespace and device state lives in the KABI reserves or existing holes, and the fields are hidden from genksyms.

Carry the netns_ipv4 l3mdev placement and its static_asserts here
(previously in the trailing KMI patch): IPVLAN selects
NET_L3_MASTER_DEV, so the fields must never be built at their stock
conditional positions. Enable the nftables, bridge netfilter, IPv6
NAT, IPVS/SCTP, tunnel, virtual NIC and tc options in gki_defconfig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
